CHECKKKK
One thing to fix on your side
10 of your 22 Vercel env vars are not exposed to the Preview environment — SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET, and the seven POSTGRES_* vars (all Production-only). The NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* pair is on Preview, so the app will likely render, but anything reading those server-side names will break on Preview only. In Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables, tick Preview on those (pointing at a staging DB if you'd rather previews not touch live data). I didn't change them — that's a data-access decision, and re-scoping them to a live database is your call.

